// PIN (kebab-stdlib-restructure): `std/io:println` is DELETED — subsumed by
// `print.ln` (it was just a non-interpolating nerf). Calling it must become a
// frontend error (unknown symbol). RED today — println still exists and this
// compiles cleanly, so no error is produced and EXPECT fails. Greenfield: the
// old form must fail loudly once removed. Uses the current `.`-path form to
// isolate the missing-symbol reason from the separate `/`-namespace change.
import std/io

~std.io:println(text: "println should be gone")
